-gt -ob -v -f palette256 -cm 8 -t0x
# NOTE: architectds only reads the first line of a .ptxc, so the arguments must
# come first and everything below is just documentation.
#
# Black variant of the menu font, converted for the top-screen text layer (see
# TopScreenText). palette256 output is a linear 8bpp index map — the same layout
# an 8bpp bitmap BG and libdsf's DSF_BMP_RGB256 expect — unlike the tex4x4 build
# of DejaVuSans-Bold_0.png, which is a 3D texture for the bottom-screen menu.
# The glyph shape lives in the PNG's alpha channel (its RGB is black
# everywhere), and paletted DS formats carry 1-bit alpha, so -t0x pins index 0
# as the transparent slot and the glyphs come out hard-edged (alpha >= 128).
# -ob (not -og) yields _tex.bin + _pal.bin, which TopScreenText freads directly.
